			<div class="content" id="post-content-4844861">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre:</strong> Drama, History</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> A demonic, non-corporeal entity formerly of divine origin that turned on humanity following a failed GOC neutralization attempt in the 1960s. The entity has limited control over the collective human psyche and has been worshipped by various ancient civilizations as a deity associated with love (Cupid/Eros, Bastet, Freyja, etc). After its fall, it began inflicting deleterious effects on the collective human unconsciousness most clearly observable in secular societies that could gradually lead to an IK-Class Collapse of Global Civilization Scenario if left unchecked. Symptoms include declining birth and marriage rates, increasing divorce and abortion rates, anxiety, low self-esteem, suicidal tendencies, and family breakdowns.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> A joint operation by the GOC, Foundation, and a handful of Serpent's Hand defectors led to the creation of the &quot;Valentia Protocol&quot;, which trapped themselves and the entity in a stalemate. It's fueled by people's faith in love, which it actively works to destroy. If the Foundation does nothing it would destroy itself but with disastrous repercussions on the human psyche. By keeping it alive they can mitigate the risk to mankind but are likely only prolonging the inevitable. The primary goal is to buy enough time to find a permanent solution to its elaborate murder-suicide attempt.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> The &quot;Valentia Protocol&quot; reveals that the proliferation and spread of Valentine's Day throughout the global community since the late 20th century is a Foundation psyop to counteract its effects. Despite displaying moderate success, this is only a temporary solution until the entity can be appeased, contained, or properly neutralized. Direct manipulation of the collective unconsciousness could have been utilized as a potential workaround if not for the obvious ethical implications as well as all research regarding this endeavor having been (allegedly) destroyed following the SCP-5000 incident.</p>

							</div>

								
