			<div class="content" id="post-content-4846469">
									

<p>The original intent for the story was that I was going to leave it open-ended; the beginning essentially takes real-world recent history and views it through a fantastic lens. The idea was that the stalemate is still ongoing but appears to be losing effectiveness as time progresses (utilizing events such as Japan's birthrate reaching its lowest recorded number last year and America's marriage rates reaching a record low the year before as evidence). I was trying to convey a sort of &quot;optimism vs fatalism&quot; theme and potentially write some supplementary Tales to explore the different possibilities in which it could end.<br />
As for how I would tell the story, I planned to use a series of missives and message &amp; interview logs to highlight the conflicting and shared ideals of the different factions in their interactions with each other.</p>

