			<div class="content" id="post-content-4864850">
									

<p>You mostly got it right, the celebration of Valentine's Day as a whole essentially is the ritual. The more people that celebrate it, the less damage the fallen god does. Here's a rough outline of how I picture the story progressing, I just found out &quot;What Is Love&quot; was already taken by 031 so I'll come up with a different title later.</p>
<p><strong>Object Class:</strong> Euclid, as the containment procedures relatively don't require much work on the Foundation's part.</p>
<p><strong>Special Containment Procedures:</strong> It's stated here that the Valentia Protocol must be enacted on an annual basis at all costs, and low-level memetic agents are to be disseminated within advertising in all known forms of media with ethics committee approval of regime change operations in [REDACTED (several Middle Eastern countries that banned V-day)] in conjunction with the United States government currently pending.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Description</strong>: The section begins with a seemingly unrelated Foundation investigation in 1965 into the ritualistic suicides of Bronze Age archaeologists following expeditions into Jordan leading to the discovery of SCP-5XXX-1, the ruins of a civilization that displeased the entity in the past and consequently collapsed in on itself as a result with the lingering effects inflicting severe anxiety, low self-esteem, and suicidal tendencies on anyone within proximity too low on the Psionic Resistance Index to resist it. Further attempts to gain insight into its nature eventually resulted in the capture of SH saboteurs attempting to stop them from disturbing its “resting place” and the Foundation being alerted to the existence of SCP-5XXX.</p>
<p><strong>Interview Log 1</strong>: Discussion between a captured SH operative and a Foundation researcher regarding the GOC termination attempt in early 1953 spearheaded by occultists who would later go on to form The United Church of Satan, Scientist. The next two decades were marked by escalating conflicts between SH cells that worshipped the deity seeking revenge and the GOC. SCP's supposed neutralization called into question.</p>
<p><strong>Description continued</strong>: Reiteration of the elevator pitch</p>
<p><strong>Interview Log 2</strong>: Communication between the Foundation and GOC attempting to confirm the neutralization of the entity, statistics utilized by the Foundation to disprove their claims, distrust on both sides leads to little progress.</p>
<p><strong>Incident Log 1</strong>: Several members from the subsections of the three organizations involved in the investigation are found to have killed themselves and/or others.</p>
<p><strong>Interview Log 3</strong>: Three-way communication between the organizations, with the Foundation essentially acting as a mediator several times throughout. Valentia Protocol established.</p>
<p><strong>Experiment Log 1</strong>: Valentia enacted in Sweden, 1966. Marriage rates continue to decline, divorce rates continue to climb, failure.</p>
<p><strong>Experiment Log 2</strong>: Valentia enacted in Japan, 1970. Initial results show promise.</p>
<p><strong>Experiment Log 3</strong>: India, 1992. Massive success.</p>
<p><strong>Experiment Log 4</strong>: Pakistan, 1996. Moderate success, government interference complicating data collection.</p>
<p><strong>Experiment Log 4</strong>: Iran, 2009. [REDACTED]</p>
<p><strong>Incident Log 2</strong>: A valentine's card is left on the project head's desk on Valentine's Day 2014, reading &quot;If you all ever really loved me you'd let me die.&quot; Global decline continues.</p>
</div>
